who's received the cold treatment.

543
00:22:58,461 --> 00:23:02,632
That's totally the type of thing men say.

544
00:23:02,715 --> 00:23:04,842
I haven't been that cold.

545
00:23:04,926 --> 00:23:06,094
I don't know.

546
00:23:06,177 --> 00:23:08,054
I swear, I haven't been that cold.

547
00:23:11,808 --> 00:23:13,726
I see.

548
00:23:13,810 --> 00:23:16,145
That was a sudden revelation.

549
00:23:16,229 --> 00:23:17,980
It came out of nowhere.

550
00:23:18,064 --> 00:23:19,065
I got pretty loud.

551
00:23:19,148 --> 00:23:22,485
So Hiroyoshi-san's X is Yoko-san.

552
00:23:22,568 --> 00:23:25,321
You, you mentioned something
when they were talking.

553
00:23:25,404 --> 00:23:27,323
Something about men.

554
00:23:27,406 --> 00:23:30,409
It's not just Hiroyoshi,

555
00:23:31,035 --> 00:23:34,622
there are so many men like that.

556
00:23:34,705 --> 00:23:39,210
He's still acting clingy
even after breaking up.

557
00:23:39,293 --> 00:23:40,545
Same with Hikaru-san.

558
00:23:40,628 --> 00:23:42,130
Like the woman should know them better.

559
00:23:42,213 --> 00:23:44,549
They all think "You're my woman."

560
00:23:44,632 --> 00:23:47,844
He might still have some feelings for her.

561
00:23:47,927 --> 00:23:52,140
But Yoko-san would do things
like praise him to a point

562
00:23:52,598 --> 00:23:54,684
where it makes him think that.

563
00:23:54,767 --> 00:23:59,647
She told him that being vulnerable
in front of everyone was strength,

564
00:23:59,730 --> 00:24:00,648
And admirable.

565
00:24:00,731 --> 00:24:04,443
As a man, you'd pause and think about it.

566
00:24:04,527 --> 00:24:07,029
All men would stop and think, right?

567
00:24:08,823 --> 00:24:09,991
What's wrong with that?

568
00:24:10,074 --> 00:24:11,409
So positive.

569
00:24:11,492 --> 00:24:12,827
90% of the time, you're wrong!

570
00:24:12,910 --> 00:24:13,995
Really?

571
00:24:14,078 --> 00:24:15,121
That much?

572
00:24:15,204 --> 00:24:20,668
Now, Yoko-san is being pursued by Satoshi,
a man 11 years her junior.

573
00:24:20,751 --> 00:24:23,212
What do you two think about their pace?

574
00:24:23,296 --> 00:24:27,592
It could be fine
if they both have the same pace.

575
00:24:27,675 --> 00:24:33,639
But it's probably too soon to tell
if their paces match.

576
00:24:34,265 --> 00:24:37,602
If I was pursued like that,
I might be taken aback.

577
00:24:37,685 --> 00:24:41,731
So Satoshi mistakenly assumed
Yoko's X was Daichi.

578
00:24:41,814 --> 00:24:46,319
I bet that's why Satoshi-san was panicked,
that she was trying to get back together.

579
00:24:46,402 --> 00:24:50,072
It's easy to imagine that you would have
no chance if that's the case.

580
00:24:50,156 --> 00:24:54,493
So he wanted to come out
and tell her he was interested in her too.

581
00:24:54,577 --> 00:24:56,370
That explains the panic.

582
00:24:56,454 --> 00:24:57,872
You're a Love Transit pro.

583
00:24:59,624 --> 00:25:02,585
We got a girl's night, tonight. Yes!

584
00:25:02,668 --> 00:25:04,045
This is great.

585
00:25:04,128 --> 00:25:06,589
Cheers.

586
00:25:08,132 --> 00:25:11,844
You know those roses.

587
00:25:11,928 --> 00:25:14,764
The blue roses? I was married to my X.

588
00:25:15,640 --> 00:25:17,308
I have kids, too.

589
00:25:18,559 --> 00:25:19,602
In high school.

590
00:25:20,895 --> 00:25:23,564
So two out of five are Mao and her X.

591
00:25:23,648 --> 00:25:24,690
Right here.

592
00:25:25,233 --> 00:25:26,734
Yoko?

593
00:25:26,817 --> 00:25:27,777
I've been married.

594
00:25:27,860 --> 00:25:30,112
I had a feeling it was you.

595
00:25:30,196 --> 00:25:31,572
But not your X?

596
00:25:31,656 --> 00:25:32,907
Not my X.

597
00:25:32,990 --> 00:25:34,825
So Yoko-san was married
to someone who wasn't X.

598
00:25:34,909 --> 00:25:36,118
I see.

599
00:25:36,202 --> 00:25:37,662
How old were you?

600
00:25:37,745 --> 00:25:39,914
I was 25.

601
00:25:39,997 --> 00:25:41,207
That's young.

602
00:25:41,874 --> 00:25:45,544
I had my child at 26,
so my kid is already 21 and in college.

603
00:25:46,545 --> 00:25:47,463
Wow.

604
00:25:47,546 --> 00:25:48,673
-Such a young mom.
-One?

605
00:25:48,756 --> 00:25:49,715
-So young.
-Just one.

606
00:25:49,799 --> 00:25:50,800
So young.

607
00:25:50,883 --> 00:25:53,594
Is dating as a single mom really hard?

608
00:25:53,678 --> 00:25:57,265
It's hard, because there's nothing
more important than my son.

609
00:25:57,348 --> 00:25:58,849
Exactly!

610
00:26:00,142 --> 00:26:01,727
Why did you break up with X?

611
00:26:01,811 --> 00:26:03,771
The reason we broke up
was his ill-chosen remarks.

612
00:26:03,854 --> 00:26:05,606
-Remarks?
-Remarks?

613
00:26:05,690 --> 00:26:08,567
There were a lot.

614
00:26:08,651 --> 00:26:11,362
And the remarks just added up.

615
00:26:11,862 --> 00:26:14,532
Like he would say the things
I didn't want to hear

616
00:26:15,074 --> 00:26:19,495
at all the exact wrong moments.

617
00:26:19,954 --> 00:26:22,456
And it wasn't just once.

618
00:26:22,540 --> 00:26:25,293
I was a huge tiger mom,

619
00:26:25,876 --> 00:26:27,461
even choosing my son's career.

620
00:26:27,545 --> 00:26:31,590
I told him you are either becoming
a doctor, lawyer, or pilot.

621
00:26:32,341 --> 00:26:36,721
And basically dictated which school
and what career he could have.

622
00:26:37,179 --> 00:26:40,057
But it caused him to have
a mental breakdown.

623
00:26:40,141 --> 00:26:42,685
I'm going to cry.

624
00:26:43,477 --> 00:26:44,603
It's making me remember.

625
00:26:44,687 --> 00:26:47,815
We've got tons of tissues just for you.

626
00:26:47,898 --> 00:26:48,983
They have your name on them.

627
00:26:49,066 --> 00:26:54,780
So he ended up not being able to go
to any of the schools because of me.

628
00:26:56,407 --> 00:26:57,533
It was my fault.

629
00:26:57,616 --> 00:27:01,787
And I was with X around that time.

630
00:27:02,872 --> 00:27:06,751
But as expected,
he just didn't understand.

631
00:27:16,427 --> 00:27:20,556
I got pregnant fairly soon
after getting married.

632
00:27:21,307 --> 00:27:23,559
And quickly after that,

633
00:27:23,642 --> 00:27:28,356
my husband fell for another woman,
and we divorced.

634
00:27:41,619 --> 00:27:47,708
My best friend had a birthday gathering,

635
00:27:47,792 --> 00:27:51,212
and we just happened to meet
by coincidence.

636
00:27:51,295 --> 00:27:54,090
I met Yoko-san when I was still married.

637
00:27:54,173 --> 00:27:55,925
However, we were already separated.

638
00:27:56,008 --> 00:28:01,097
I didn't want her to become my affair
partner when I saw a future for us.

639
00:28:02,556 --> 00:28:06,936
Separated from his ex-wife
while contemplating divorce…

640
00:28:07,019 --> 00:28:11,148
When I decided to date her after giving
divorce a serious consideration,

641
00:28:11,232 --> 00:28:13,859
I could see myself spending
the rest of my life with her.

642
00:28:15,069 --> 00:28:17,738
After having a clean break
from my ex-wife.

643
00:28:18,197 --> 00:28:22,284
I confessed my feelings after waiting
a year following my divorce.

644
00:28:24,120 --> 00:28:27,039
"If I had to describe you in one word,
it would be sincere.

645
00:28:27,123 --> 00:28:30,918
"Your demeanor is elegant,
and always perfect on dates.

646
00:28:31,001 --> 00:28:34,338
"Every time, our dates
felt like they were from the movies."

647
00:28:40,886 --> 00:28:44,640
But during that time…

648
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:47,768
My son stopped going to school.

649
00:28:47,852 --> 00:28:53,607
That sent me into a depression
that lasted about two or three years.

650
00:28:53,691 --> 00:28:58,904
And during that time,
Hiroyoshi-san without meaning to upset me,

651
00:28:59,363 --> 00:29:04,535
asked me something like will we ever
get married while this is going on.

652
00:29:04,618 --> 00:29:07,663
It just came out.

653
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:12,668
That single comment
really closed the door shut.

654
00:29:28,976 --> 00:29:30,978
So, I'm the one who invited you to this.

655
00:29:31,479 --> 00:29:34,857
When I started talking
about some specifics, you hesitated.

656
00:29:34,940 --> 00:29:38,319
I did. I mean, participating in this,

657
00:29:38,402 --> 00:29:42,198
the biggest issue for me is the idea
of having to see things I don't want to,

658
00:29:42,281 --> 00:29:46,619
like you starting a new romance
with some other guy.

659
00:29:47,453 --> 00:29:51,916
But in the end, how often
am I meeting someone like you,

660
00:29:53,083 --> 00:29:57,254
so a part of me wasn't able
to simply move on.

661
00:29:58,088 --> 00:30:00,633
It's like I've been chasing it all along.

662
00:30:02,051 --> 00:30:06,347
Deep down, I'm leaning
90 to 95% towards reconciliation.

663
00:30:06,430 --> 00:30:09,934
I meet a lot of women,

664
00:30:11,852 --> 00:30:15,189
but nobody I've been
drawn to as much as her.

665
00:30:16,065 --> 00:30:19,902
Honestly, I don't know how much
I should say to you.

666
00:30:20,903 --> 00:30:23,280
Since I'm wanting to get
back together with you.

667
00:30:23,781 --> 00:30:28,327
The biggest thing, is that I don't want
anybody taking you away from me.

668
00:30:28,702 --> 00:30:32,998
I still want to do things
over with you again,

669
00:30:33,082 --> 00:30:34,750
which is why I followed you here.

670
00:30:35,668 --> 00:30:38,629
And even though I knew this hocance

671
00:30:38,712 --> 00:30:42,132
would be a pretty big ordeal for me,

672
00:30:43,092 --> 00:30:45,261
when someone I care about
invites me to it,

673
00:30:46,011 --> 00:30:49,807
I didn't think I could say no,
so I sucked it up.

674
00:30:49,890 --> 00:30:53,394
I was hoping you could at least
understand that a little bit.

675
00:30:55,854 --> 00:30:58,274
I see.

676
00:30:58,357 --> 00:31:01,902
Each layer is so heavy.

677
00:31:01,986 --> 00:31:07,449
So yes, Hiroyoshi-san and Yoko-san
are Xs as everyone suspected.

678
00:31:07,533 --> 00:31:09,702
They're different
from Mao-san and Hikaru-san

679
00:31:09,785 --> 00:31:15,958
because they started dating as divorcees.

680
00:31:16,041 --> 00:31:19,587
Having a child involved is big.

681
00:31:19,670 --> 00:31:23,299
That becomes key.

682
00:31:23,382 --> 00:31:28,596
Also, Hiroyoshi-san already expressed
his desire to get back together.

683
00:31:28,679 --> 00:31:33,350
So now, I'm curious where Satoshi
is going to take things from here.

684
00:31:33,434 --> 00:31:36,312
Yeah, since Satoshi
is really going after her.

685
00:31:36,395 --> 00:31:40,566
I wonder how Satoshi will react
if he gets wind of this.

686
00:31:40,649 --> 00:31:43,527
I'm just imagining
so many things right now.

687
00:31:43,611 --> 00:31:47,072
Satoshi is probably feeling jealous
of Yoko's X right now.

688
00:31:47,156 --> 00:31:48,157
I'd say so.

689
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:52,911
Now it's going to come as a shock
to him when the 36-year-old Satoshi

690
00:31:52,995 --> 00:31:58,167
learns Yoko-san has a 21-year-old son.

691
00:31:58,250 --> 00:32:00,711
I can see him letting out
a big exclamation.

692
00:32:00,794 --> 00:32:02,713
He's going to be surprised for sure.

693
00:32:02,796 --> 00:32:05,924
It's not irrelevant if they're going
to spend their lives together.

694
00:32:06,008 --> 00:32:09,762
Does he have the grace
to be able to accept it all?

695
00:32:10,679 --> 00:32:13,223
Especially since that's where
Hiroyoshi-san went wrong,

696
00:32:13,307 --> 00:32:15,851
crossing the line with his remarks.

697
00:32:15,934 --> 00:32:18,604
Since even Hiroyoshi-san
ended up like that.

698
00:32:18,687 --> 00:32:22,191
Would Satoshi-san do something similar?

699
00:32:22,274 --> 00:32:24,526
It's hard to say.

700
00:32:24,985 --> 00:32:27,863
Before joining the show,

701
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:32,326
I thought I'd get asked out on dates
more than this.

702
00:32:32,409 --> 00:32:33,369
You did?

703
00:32:33,452 --> 00:32:35,537
But I got the wrong idea.

704
00:32:35,621 --> 00:32:40,668
I was the one invited here by my X,
but he hasn't invited me on any dates,

705
00:32:40,751 --> 00:32:43,671
-or the lounge, or to talk on the balcony.
-You're scaring me.

706
00:32:43,754 --> 00:32:45,297
So like, why did you even
invite me on here?

707
00:32:45,381 --> 00:32:46,298
Kanako's sulking.

708
00:32:46,382 --> 00:32:48,842
Okay, the first day was short.
I can understand. But the second day?

709
00:32:48,926 --> 00:32:49,885
Still nothing.

710
00:32:49,968 --> 00:32:52,805
Day three, still nothing. Go to hell.

711
00:32:58,018 --> 00:33:01,063
But I think that's cute, Kanako.

712
00:33:01,146 --> 00:33:03,691
Because it means you have enough feelings
for him to get mad like that.

713
00:33:03,774 --> 00:33:05,109
That's the impression you get.

714
00:33:05,192 --> 00:33:06,026
That's true.

715
00:33:06,110 --> 00:33:06,985
If you had no feelings…

716
00:33:07,069 --> 00:33:07,945
So you have feelings.

717
00:33:08,028 --> 00:33:09,905
Satoshi?

718
00:33:09,988 --> 00:33:12,366
They are close in age. It's possible.

719
00:33:12,449 --> 00:33:13,867
I bet it's Satoshi.

720
00:33:13,951 --> 00:33:16,245
Why do you think he invited you?

721
00:33:16,328 --> 00:33:18,622
I mean, it's such a downer.

722
00:33:19,248 --> 00:33:22,501
Do you think he asked you here
to reconcile?

723
00:33:22,584 --> 00:33:23,836
I've never dated.

724
00:33:24,294 --> 00:33:26,839
What, like any guys?

725
00:33:26,922 --> 00:33:28,716
No, I've never dated my X.

726
00:33:29,341 --> 00:33:31,009
Wait, what does that mean?

727
00:33:31,093 --> 00:33:32,469
What's that now?

728
00:33:32,553 --> 00:33:34,555
I've never dated X.

729
00:33:34,638 --> 00:33:36,974
What!

730
00:33:37,057 --> 00:33:38,100
Is that allowed?

731
00:33:38,183 --> 00:33:40,477
What do you mean?

732
00:33:42,563 --> 00:33:44,064
I don't understand.

733
00:33:44,148 --> 00:33:45,399
Doesn't this break the system?

734
00:33:45,482 --> 00:33:46,734
What's she mean?

735
00:34:11,258 --> 00:34:12,259
Long time no see.

736
00:34:12,342 --> 00:34:13,385
I knew it was Satoshi.

737
00:34:13,469 --> 00:34:14,762
It's Satoshi.

738
00:34:15,554 --> 00:34:16,764
Long time no see.

739
00:34:21,351 --> 00:34:22,394
This is crazy.

740
00:34:22,478 --> 00:34:23,520
Yeah.

741
00:34:23,604 --> 00:34:25,189
This is crazy.

742
00:34:25,731 --> 00:34:26,857
It feels so strange.

743
00:34:26,940 --> 00:34:28,150
Yeah.

744
00:34:29,902 --> 00:34:31,570
So this show,

745
00:34:32,571 --> 00:34:37,618
isn't it about ex-boyfriends
and ex-girlfriends?

746
00:34:37,701 --> 00:34:38,744
Yeah.

747
00:34:39,328 --> 00:34:40,871
Were we dating?

748
00:34:45,042 --> 00:34:46,627
In my mind,

749
00:34:48,128 --> 00:34:50,088
we weren't dating.

750
00:34:51,548 --> 00:34:53,342
So Satoshi tends to get ahead of himself.

751
00:34:53,425 --> 00:34:54,551
Did he think they were?

752
00:34:54,635 --> 00:34:57,846
He must have thought they were together.

753
00:34:57,930 --> 00:35:00,182
I mean, you never confessed
your feelings to me.

754
00:35:01,475 --> 00:35:02,935
Like a declaration of love.

755
00:35:05,062 --> 00:35:06,730
I guess he thought we were together.

756
00:35:06,814 --> 00:35:10,609
But in my mind,
that never counted as dating.

757
00:35:10,692 --> 00:35:13,904
From my point of view,
I thought we were together.

758
00:35:13,987 --> 00:35:15,113
They're not on the same page.

759
00:35:15,197 --> 00:35:18,909
We had dinner and drinks,

760
00:35:21,161 --> 00:35:24,331
and I walked her back to her place

761
00:35:25,290 --> 00:35:27,125
where I told her how I felt.

762
00:35:28,418 --> 00:35:31,338
And she gave me the okay.

763
00:35:31,797 --> 00:35:33,549
So that's the day we started dating.

764
00:35:34,466 --> 00:35:35,801
And that was January.

765
00:35:35,884 --> 00:35:40,806
Then there was about a three-month period

766
00:35:41,265 --> 00:35:43,392
where we couldn't see each other.

767
00:35:44,643 --> 00:35:47,271
He asked if he could come over,
and I said no.

768
00:35:47,354 --> 00:35:49,523
He asked me to come over to his place,
and I said no.

769
00:35:49,606 --> 00:35:50,440
For real?

770
00:35:50,524 --> 00:35:53,026
We seriously haven't done anything.

771
00:35:54,403 --> 00:35:56,446
Is this a horror show now?

772
00:35:57,281 --> 00:35:58,323
What is this?

773
00:35:58,907 --> 00:36:03,453
Then things just sort of fizzled out.

774
00:36:04,162 --> 00:36:07,666
That took place over

775
00:36:07,749 --> 00:36:11,628
about a two or three month period.

776
00:36:12,546 --> 00:36:16,508
I'm shocked to learn

777
00:36:16,592 --> 00:36:22,014
that when I told her I liked her then,
it didn't register for her.

778
00:36:22,097 --> 00:36:25,475
We don't know who will end up
becoming a couple.

779
00:36:26,518 --> 00:36:30,022
There's a chance
I won't end up with anyone at all,

780
00:36:31,273 --> 00:36:34,526
but I'd like to find a good love.

781
00:36:35,360 --> 00:36:37,446
That goes without saying.

782
00:36:37,529 --> 00:36:39,948
Kanako, you're perfectly normal.

783
00:36:41,366 --> 00:36:45,662
I guess I have no choice
but start from scratch.

784
00:36:57,424 --> 00:36:58,926
He watched this on the first day?

785
00:36:59,009 --> 00:37:01,178
And he's watching Kana-chan's.

786
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:13,649
In percentage terms, it's 50%.

787
00:37:19,655 --> 00:37:21,657
Why did you decide to participate?

788
00:37:21,740 --> 00:37:25,410
I suddenly got the feeling
like I really wanted to fall in love now.

789
00:37:25,911 --> 00:37:29,039
I've completely moved on from all
my past relationships at this point,

790
00:37:29,122 --> 00:37:34,086
and if someone came along,
I'd like to get married in a year.

791
00:37:38,256 --> 00:37:39,299
That'd be ideal.

792
00:37:46,598 --> 00:37:52,771
Having watched her video,

793
00:37:54,398 --> 00:37:57,275
my instincts told me
she wasn't interested in me at all.

794
00:37:58,485 --> 00:38:04,032
Judging from her expression and vibe,
that's what I took from it.

795
00:38:05,701 --> 00:38:09,413
I think she mentioned she was 50-50
about getting back together.

796
00:38:10,914 --> 00:38:13,917
But I sensed she didn't really mean it.

797
00:38:15,877 --> 00:38:18,547
I got the sense

798
00:38:21,550 --> 00:38:23,385
that she was excited to find a new love.

799
00:38:23,468 --> 00:38:28,515
I was shocked that it didn't seem like
I was part of her future.

800
00:38:28,598 --> 00:38:31,226
I bet it was.

801
00:38:31,309 --> 00:38:34,646
I was originally interested
in getting back together with Kanako-san.

802
00:38:34,730 --> 00:38:39,484
I wasn't imagining asking
anyone else out or anything.

803
00:38:41,028 --> 00:38:44,948
So Satoshi invited Kanako
on the show to pursue her, right?

804
00:38:45,032 --> 00:38:47,159
But he's going after Yoko so hard.

805
00:38:53,081 --> 00:38:55,208
I'll be here all day.

806
00:38:55,792 --> 00:38:57,627
I haven't gone anywhere.

807
00:38:59,755 --> 00:39:01,298
I'm hungry.

808
00:39:03,842 --> 00:39:05,302
I'm irritated.

809
00:39:05,385 --> 00:39:08,972
It's the fourth day already.
And I still haven't been asked out.

810
00:39:10,140 --> 00:39:14,853
It's like, why did you even
invite me to this hocance at all?

811
00:39:14,936 --> 00:39:17,022
I totally get where she's coming from.

812
00:39:17,105 --> 00:39:18,023
On the balcony?

813
00:39:18,106 --> 00:39:19,232
Yeah, let's go.

814
00:39:29,326 --> 00:39:31,036
Do you want to go to the lounge?

815
00:39:31,119 --> 00:39:32,579
Yeah? Sure.

816
00:39:32,662 --> 00:39:33,705
Have fun.

817
00:39:34,289 --> 00:39:37,334
Bye then.

818
00:39:40,962 --> 00:39:44,049
Satoshi-san invited Mao-san,

819
00:39:44,132 --> 00:39:47,052
and on top of that, he asked her to go
to the lounge in front of me.

820
00:39:47,135 --> 00:39:51,014
I was like, when is he finally
going to invite me?

821
00:39:52,057 --> 00:39:54,434
Because there was no way
I was going to ask him out.

822
00:39:55,227 --> 00:39:57,646
He was pretty touchy-feely with everyone.

823
00:39:58,605 --> 00:39:59,773
Touching their shoulders.

824
00:40:00,857 --> 00:40:02,901
I was like, "Okay."

825
00:40:08,281 --> 00:40:11,451
I was with her.

826
00:40:11,535 --> 00:40:13,912
We went on a seaside date.

827
00:40:13,995 --> 00:40:14,830
Wow.

828
00:40:18,667 --> 00:40:22,003
I think that annoyed me the most.

829
00:40:23,505 --> 00:40:28,593
We were playing blind man's bluff, and the
winner invited someone to the lounge.

830
00:40:28,677 --> 00:40:30,011
And Satoshi-san won.

831
00:40:30,095 --> 00:40:31,805
One, two, thee, show.

832
00:40:31,888 --> 00:40:33,348
Wow!

833
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:36,560
So I guess, pick someone to go with.

834
00:40:36,643 --> 00:40:37,477
Right.

835
00:40:38,270 --> 00:40:39,146
Misato-chan.

836
00:40:39,229 --> 00:40:40,689
Really?

837
00:40:40,772 --> 00:40:42,023
Have fun.

838
00:40:42,107 --> 00:40:44,025
That was unexpected. Really?

839
00:40:45,026 --> 00:40:47,863
I was like, you're going
out with a different woman again?

840
00:40:49,239 --> 00:40:51,199
I was about to snap.

841
00:40:54,411 --> 00:40:55,745
Cheers.

842
00:40:55,829 --> 00:40:56,830
Your first lounge visit?

843
00:40:56,913 --> 00:40:58,456
First time at the lounge!

844
00:41:00,750 --> 00:41:02,794
He's inviting everyone
out except for Kanako-san.

845
00:41:02,878 --> 00:41:04,004
For real?

846
00:41:04,087 --> 00:41:05,046
What is this?

847
00:41:13,805 --> 00:41:16,057
It happened yesterday and today.

848
00:41:17,142 --> 00:41:20,937
She was trying to end
everyone's time at the hocance

849
00:41:23,481 --> 00:41:27,527
as quickly as possible.

850
00:41:29,571 --> 00:41:33,074
So I'd like everyone's help.

851
00:41:33,158 --> 00:41:34,117
Okay, thanks.

852
00:41:34,201 --> 00:41:35,452
I'm really sorry.

853
00:41:35,535 --> 00:41:37,037
Thank you.

854
00:41:37,662 --> 00:41:38,955
Have a seat.

855
00:41:39,998 --> 00:41:43,126
Sit down? I feel it's easier
being on my feet.

856
00:41:44,836 --> 00:41:48,173
Thanks, Satoshi. Sorry about this.

857
00:41:50,425 --> 00:41:52,969
You know, just speak up
if you have something going on.

858
00:41:53,053 --> 00:41:54,638
Excuse me.

859
00:41:54,721 --> 00:41:57,265
It's already 11:30, so everyone gather up.

860
00:41:57,349 --> 00:41:59,059
I thought we had time.

861
00:41:59,142 --> 00:42:01,853
Well then, thank you,
let's call it a night.

862
00:42:01,937 --> 00:42:03,563
Oh, okay!

863
00:42:05,649 --> 00:42:09,819
I mean, I don't see what's wrong
with calling it a day at 11:30.

864
00:42:09,903 --> 00:42:11,196
Yeah.

865
00:42:11,279 --> 00:42:15,367
She's like "Wrap it up,
let's all go home, and go to sleep."

866
00:42:15,450 --> 00:42:17,410
She's trying to keep things moving.

867
00:42:17,911 --> 00:42:21,248
And that stance
is the complete opposite of me.

868
00:42:24,084 --> 00:42:25,043
You know.

869
00:42:26,586 --> 00:42:30,840
Yes, I know time is limited.

870
00:42:33,260 --> 00:42:38,181
The X in my mind

871
00:42:38,265 --> 00:42:42,477
was someone cool who would
be up for anything like playing cards.

872
00:42:42,560 --> 00:42:44,938
I thought she was someone

873
00:42:45,021 --> 00:42:49,567
who had a more flexible mindset.

874
00:42:54,781 --> 00:42:55,782
It's crazy.

875
00:42:56,449 --> 00:42:57,867
He's crying.

876
00:43:06,376 --> 00:43:09,254
I mean, right after Hiroyoshi
bared his heart to us,

877
00:43:11,381 --> 00:43:15,427
she just tried to wrap things up
and call it a night.

878
00:43:16,678 --> 00:43:17,846
It just honestly…

879
00:43:25,103 --> 00:43:27,480
didn't sit well with me.

880
00:43:28,815 --> 00:43:32,569
It's not something I would be able to do.

881
00:43:33,236 --> 00:43:39,576
And how casually X was able to do that,

882
00:43:39,659 --> 00:43:42,954
I really hated it, you know.

883
00:43:45,165 --> 00:43:46,166
Like…

884
00:43:49,127 --> 00:43:51,338
If she was the X I thought she was,

885
00:43:52,672 --> 00:43:57,510
I imagined she would've gone
by his side to comfort him.

886
00:43:58,803 --> 00:43:59,763
Yeah.

887
00:44:03,975 --> 00:44:08,229
And that was painful to me,
because she's my X.

888
00:44:11,691 --> 00:44:13,818
Is he okay?

889
00:44:13,902 --> 00:44:16,529
We're working with a bunch
of unique personalities.

890
00:44:16,613 --> 00:44:18,990
I think we need to take a moment
to break things down.

891
00:44:19,074 --> 00:44:20,950
Allow me to review.

892
00:44:21,034 --> 00:44:25,205
Satoshi has invited Kanako
here to this hocance.

893
00:44:25,288 --> 00:44:30,919
On the day they reunited, we learned that
Kanako never considered them to be dating.

894
00:44:31,002 --> 00:44:36,841
According to Satoshi, he expressed his
feelings to her, and she acknowledged it.

895
00:44:36,925 --> 00:44:40,428
Kanako saw things differently, and they
never even went to each other's homes.

896
00:44:40,512 --> 00:44:43,598
She maintains they were not
romantically involved at all.

897
00:44:43,681 --> 00:44:48,728
Now, Satoshi invited her to the hocance
to rekindle a romance with her,

898
00:44:48,812 --> 00:44:51,648
but what he saw of Kanako
left him completely disillusioned.

899
00:44:51,731 --> 00:44:57,362
As a result, Kanako is getting irritated
by Satoshi who invited her here.

900
00:44:57,445 --> 00:45:01,074
The fact that he's been
asking out all the other women,

901
00:45:01,157 --> 00:45:05,078
asking them to the lounge
within earshot of Kanako.

902
00:45:05,161 --> 00:45:08,373
It sounds like he's partly motivated

903
00:45:08,456 --> 00:45:10,333
by trying to get back at her a little.

904
00:45:10,417 --> 00:45:11,835
So one thing I thought,

905
00:45:11,918 --> 00:45:16,131
Satoshi is saying he's totally
disillusioned by her.

906
00:45:16,214 --> 00:45:18,675
Kanako-san could just take initiative
and act on her own.

907
00:45:19,676 --> 00:45:25,682
It seems like Kanako-chan
isn't the proactive aggressive type.

908
00:45:25,765 --> 00:45:27,809
She's more cute and shy.

909
00:45:27,892 --> 00:45:31,187
Also, if it's still just the fourth day,
she hasn't grasped the situation yet.

910
00:45:31,271 --> 00:45:34,023
She seems to be wondering
why a lot right now.

911
00:45:34,107 --> 00:45:36,693
So is Satoshi the weird one then?

912
00:45:38,111 --> 00:45:40,155
I mean, he's a good guy at heart.

913
00:45:40,530 --> 00:45:41,489
That's clear.

914
00:45:41,573 --> 00:45:43,992
Satoshi is so kind to Hiroyoshi.

915
00:45:44,075 --> 00:45:46,119
All the guys are so chummy.

916
00:45:46,202 --> 00:45:50,165
Then the guys should've just
gotten together on their own afterwards.

917
00:45:50,248 --> 00:45:52,917
But Kanako-san wrapped everything
up to send them home.

918
00:45:53,001 --> 00:45:54,502
That's unforgivable!

919
00:45:54,586 --> 00:45:56,254
But it's 11:30.

920
00:46:07,140 --> 00:46:08,850
This hocance is draining.

921
00:46:17,484 --> 00:46:19,444
I mean, I wanted to punch Yoko.

922
00:46:20,028 --> 00:46:21,404
That's not right, though.

923
00:46:22,113 --> 00:46:26,409
Yoko has gone through a lot in her life.

924
00:46:27,160 --> 00:46:28,745
You'd do the same in my shoes.

925
00:46:28,828 --> 00:46:31,122
No way! That's what I'm talking about.

926
00:46:33,708 --> 00:46:35,418
I'm telling you this because I wouldn't.

927
00:46:35,502 --> 00:46:37,086
But if you were me…

928
00:46:37,170 --> 00:46:39,923
I won't. I'd never do that.

929
00:46:40,590 --> 00:46:42,091
That's why I'm telling you.
